 "_clips": "Joint angles in degrees (positive turns the part counter-clockwise as seen by the camera when the character faces right: a hanging arm or leg swings forward). root_y: metres the whole body rises. loop clips run on their own clock (length_s seconds, faster with the run speed when stride_scaled); the others are posed by how far through its action the character is (0..1). Single-key clips are held poses; the body blends into them. lean_bone takes the body's lean, scaled by lean_scale. A key may carry a third entry, the easing into it: in (accelerate, for a blow landing), out (decelerate, for a wind-up or overshoot), linear; default eases both ends. blend: how fast the body moves into the clip (per second, default 18). squash: positive coils the body down and wide, negative stretches it. secondary: bones that swing on their own from the body's movement (a spring: degrees per m/s forward and falling, limits, stiffness, damping). kicks: squash given on landing and on turning round (sprung, settles on its own).",
